  ],
  "legend": {
   "only": "papers that report only this metric family",
   "other": "papers that also report another family"
  },
  "caption": "A paper with several metric families counts on each of its links, so a target's links can add up to more than its paper count.",
  "card_more": "+ {n} more",
  "card_click": "Click to list them in the Survey.",
  "card_split": "{only} report only this family · {other} also report another",
  "table_toggle": "Show as table",
  "table_caption": "Papers by target (rows) and metric family (columns). A paper counts once in every cell it has; totals are unique papers.",
  "table_total": "Papers",
  "nosurvey": "On the site this opens the Survey list at {hash} ({n} papers).",
  "link_only": "{only} of them report only this family"
 },
 "notes": [
  {
   "html": "Across all targets, ranking is the most common metric family ({met:RNK} papers), followed by calibration ({met:CAL}), and a growing number of papers evaluate decision metrics ({met:DEC}) on downstream use."
  },
  {
   "html": "Grounding sits almost entirely at the structural lens ({tl:GRD:str} of {tgt:GRD} papers), and all faithfulness methods read the semantical lens. <a href=\"#survey?cell=target.str.GRD\">See them in the coverage map</a>."
  },
  {
   "html": "Ranking is not calibration. Ranking depends only on the order of the scores, whereas calibration depends on their values: a constant uncertainty score equal to the empirical accuracy achieves zero calibration error (ECE) but gives no useful ranking, and a score can rank near-optimally while being miscalibrated. <a href=\"#playground\">Try it in the metric playground</a>."
  }
 ],
 "notes_title": "What the flow shows",
 "takeaway": {
  "n": 9,
  "title": "Target, criterion, and metric form the evaluation protocol",
  "text": "A UQ evaluation protocol evaluates the uncertainty score against a target: correctness, grounding, underspecification, or faithfulness. A distributional or semantical criterion decides whether the target is met. A metric in one of seven families measures how well the score tracks the target.",
  "sec": "§6"
 },
